    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43498" root="&#xA;                        متى&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَتَى</span></b> 
                         signifies <i>When?</i> and <i>when</i> used to denote
a condition: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنَّى</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْنَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَتَّى مَتَى</span>
                        <i>Until when? how long?</i> and also <i>until the time
when.</i> See Freytag's Arab. Prov. i. 382.

